    "id": "a29ec008e695a750",
    "title": "UK, Singapore, and Thailand central banks test cross-border FX settlement as stablecoins gain ground",
    "summary": "Project Meridian FX APAC said it demonstrated how transactions can be coordinated across conventional settlement systems and those built using blockchain technology.",
    "hasSummary": true,
    "link": "https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/11/14/uk-singapore-and-thailand-central-banks-test-cross-border-fx-settlement-as-stablecoins-gain-ground",
    "source": "CoinDesk",
    "tags": [
      "UK",
      "Singapore",
      "Thailand",
      "Project Meridian FX APAC"
    ],
    "origin": "rss",
    "pubDate": "2026-11-14T15:00:00.000Z",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-11-14T15:01:38.013Z",
    "isDuplicateOf": null,
    "content": "The central banks of the UK, Singapore, and Thailand have successfully tested cross-border foreign exchange settlement using stablecoins. Project Meridian FX APAC demonstrated how financial transactions can be effectively coordinated between conventional settlement systems and newer blockchain-based platforms, highlighting the growing role of digital assets in international banking.",
    "content_ta": "UK, Singapore மற்றும் Thailand நாடுகளின் central banks ஆகியவை stablecoins-ஐப் பயன்படுத்தி cross-border FX settlement சோதனையை வெற்றிகரமாக நடத்தியுள்ளன. Project Meridian FX APAC திட்டம், பாரம்பரிய settlement systems மற்றும் blockchain தொழில்நுட்பத்தை அடிப்படையாகக் கொண்ட புதிய தளங்களுக்கு இடையே பரிவர்த்தனைகளை எவ்வாறு ஒருங்கிணைக்க முடியும் என்பதைdemonstrate செய்துள்ளது.",
    "slug": "uk-singapore-and-thailand-central-banks-test-cross-border-fx-settlement-as-stablecoins-gain-ground"
  },
